 "result": "Added `src/routes/v2/status.ts` with `statusHandler`. I haven't run or type-checked it.\n\n- **Response:** it returns 200 with `{ status: \"ok\", uptimeSeconds, port }`. `uptimeSeconds` comes from `process.uptime()`.\n- **Port:** it reads `TEST_DAEMON_PORT` and falls back to 8089. This is the same variable `scripts/healthcheck.mjs` uses. It reports the configured port, not the one the server actually bound, so if your server is started on a different port than that variable says, the value will be wrong.\n- **Status:** it always reports `\"ok\"`. There are no dependency checks, so `\"degraded\"` and `\"down\"` are never returned.\n- **Auth:** it needs none, which suits a health probe.\n- **Wiring:** it isn't attached to a router yet. `Dashboard.tsx` expects it at `/health` and ignores the extra `port` field.",
